set up mode local in 8 steps:
  1. back up /Users/user_name/Library/LaunchAgents/local.litellm.proxy.plist to a dated copy beside it (/Users/user_name/Library/LaunchAgents/local.litellm.proxy.plist.bak-<date>-<time>, its mode without group or other bits; it keeps the old key)
  2. replace LITELLM_MASTER_KEY in /Users/user_name/Library/LaunchAgents/local.litellm.proxy.plist with a new generated key (not shown), keeping every other byte of the file; it is written without group or other bits
  3. set /Users/user_name/Library/LaunchAgents/local.litellm.proxy.plist to mode 0600 (it was 0644, readable by others; the edit already dropped those bits)
  4. set wt-model's LiteLLM pair in /Users/user_name/.config/wt-model/: url http://localhost:4000, key the new LITELLM_MASTER_KEY (not shown)
  5. restart LiteLLM so it uses the new key: launchctl kickstart -k gui/501/local.litellm.proxy
  6. wait for LiteLLM to answer at http://localhost:4000/health/liveliness and accept the new master key
  7. restart the LaunchAgent so it reads the new pair: launchctl kickstart -k gui/501/local.wt-model.serve
  8. wait for wt-model to answer at http://127.0.0.1:8787
left alone and notes:
  - keep the token file /Users/user_name/.config/wt-model/server.token
  - keep the LaunchAgent plist /Users/user_name/Library/LaunchAgents/local.wt-model.serve.plist (unchanged)
  - keep [model-server] in /Users/user_name/.config/agent-wt/config.toml (already mode = "local")
  - anything else that holds the old master key stops working once LiteLLM restarts: other clients and scripts that send it, a [litellm] api_key in /Users/user_name/.config/agent-wt/config.toml if one is set there, and copies of the plist (the backup keeps the old key; remove it once the new key works)
  - never changed in /Users/user_name/Library/LaunchAgents/local.litellm.proxy.plist: LITELLM_SALT_KEY, DATABASE_URL, provider keys and the UI login
